## Authentication

- **Admin user:** `<user>` (`<svc>_admin_user`) — delete if none is provisioned
- **Admin password:** `{global_password_prefix}_pw_<svc>` (`<svc>_admin_password`)
  — quote the EXACT var. The DB password and the admin password are often different
  secrets with confusingly similar names; check which one you are naming.
- **SSO:** `<native_oidc | header_oidc | forward_auth | none>` — read
  `files/anatomy/plugins/<svc>-base/plugin.yml` `authentik.mode`, RBAC tier
  `authentik.tier`. Say WHERE it is configured (compose env block, `occ`/API post-hook,
  or Traefik middleware) — the three behave differently on a blank.
  - Redirect URI: `<from plugin.yml redirect_uris>`
- **Autologin:** `<supports / cannot / ceiling>` — see `docs/sso-autologin-plan.md`.

## API Access

- **Base URL:** `https://<svc>{host_alias_seg}.{tenant_domain}/<api-prefix>`
- **Auth method:** `<mechanism>` — and say plainly whether nOS PROVISIONS the credential
  or a human must mint it. **Do not invent a bot account or a token path.** There is no
  `openclaw-bot` service account and no `~/agents/tokens/` tree in this estate; if your
  service has no provisioned agent credential, write that sentence instead.
- **Endpoints verified against repo source:** list the ones nOS itself calls (grep the
  role's `tasks/post.yml` and the plugin `lifecycle:` block). Mark everything else as
